From 56b00cabf2ba5323a081d027343e4f645d1b3896 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Z User <z@container>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 06:14:49 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] mwx: zero MT7902 scan dwell/timeout to match vendor connac2
 values
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The WM firmware accepts the hw-scan command (0x40003) and transmits a
probe request on the first channel, then stalls: it never hops to the
next channel and never reports MCU_EVENT_SCAN_DONE (0x0d), so no scan
results are delivered and the interface shows no networks.

The Linux vendor driver runs this exact firmware and classifies MT7902
as connac2 (is_connac2() includes is_mt7902()). On that path
mt76_connac_mcu_hw_scan() computes duration = is_connac2() ? 0 :
MT76_CONNAC_SCAN_CHANNEL_TIME, i.e. it sends timeout_value,
channel_min_dwell_time and channel_dwell_time as 0 and lets the
firmware apply its internal per-channel defaults. mwx hardcodes
120/120/4920 — the only remaining byte-level difference in the scan
request.

Zero the three timing fields for MT7902 exactly as the vendor does.
---
 SimpleMtkWlan/hal_mwx/MtkMwx.cpp | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/SimpleMtkWlan/hal_mwx/MtkMwx.cpp b/SimpleMtkWlan/hal_mwx/MtkMwx.cpp
index ba81361..4793c61 100644
--- a/SimpleMtkWlan/hal_mwx/MtkMwx.cpp
+++ b/SimpleMtkWlan/hal_mwx/MtkMwx.cpp
@@ -5533,6 +5533,20 @@ mt7921_mcu_hw_scan(struct mwx_softc *sc, int bgscan)
 	req->timeout_value = htole16(nchan * 120);
 	req->channel_min_dwell_time = htole16(120);
 	req->channel_dwell_time = htole16(120);
+	if (sc->sc_hwtype == MWX_HW_MT7902) {
+		/*
+		 * Linux mt76 puts MT7902 on the connac2 scan path and zeroes the
+		 * scan timing there (mt76_connac_mcu_hw_scan: "duration =
+		 * is_connac2() ? 0 : MT76_CONNAC_SCAN_CHANNEL_TIME"; is_connac2()
+		 * includes is_mt7902()), letting the firmware apply its internal
+		 * per-channel defaults. Nonzero dwell values stall the WM mid-scan:
+		 * one probe request goes out, then silence and no
+		 * MCU_EVENT_SCAN_DONE, so no scan results are ever delivered.
+		 */
+		req->timeout_value = 0;
+		req->channel_min_dwell_time = 0;
+		req->channel_dwell_time = 0;
+	}
 
 
